  "text": {
    "intro": "A measured length of fallen wall each, and a whole morning in which to rebuild it to the satisfaction of a judge who will push on every cope.\nFive wallers are involved. Determine each waller's finishing time, stone and feature.\n- **Waller**: Ossian Baird, Hilda Crowther, Mab Teasdale, Ewart Beck and Clem Hartley.\n- **Finishing time** (listed from earlier to later): 8am, 9am, 10am, 11am and noon.\n- **Stone**: green slate, red sandstone, Welsh rubble, Cotswold oolite and Dales limestone.\n- **Feature built**: a water smoot, a stile, a set of throughstones, a cripple hole and a lunky hole.\nEvery waller has a different finishing time, stone and feature, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "The waller who builds in a set of throughstones finishes at 11am.",
      "Ossian Baird finishes at 10am.",
      "The waller who works in Dales limestone finishes at 10am.",
      "At least one of the following holds, and possibly more than one: (a) The waller who builds in a stile and the waller who works in Cotswold oolite are exactly one hour apart in finishing time order, in one direction or the other. (b) The waller who builds in a stile and the waller who works in green slate are exactly one hour apart in finishing time order, in one direction or the other.",
      "The waller who builds in a stile and Clem Hartley are exactly one hour apart in finishing time order, in one direction or the other.",
      "Ewart Beck falls somewhere between the waller who builds in a stile and the waller who builds in a water smoot in finishing time order, matching neither.",
      "Clem Hartley is exactly one hour earlier than the waller who works in Welsh rubble, with no finishing time in between.",
      "At least one of the following holds, and possibly more than one: (a) The waller who works in red sandstone is earlier than Mab Teasdale in finishing time order. (b) Ossian Baird works in Welsh rubble.",
      "Clem Hartley is earlier than the waller who builds in a set of throughstones in finishing time order.",
      "The waller who builds in a cripple hole does not work in Cotswold oolite. Ossian Baird does not build in a cripple hole."
    ]
